liability, technical competence, calmness under pressure, cooperation, responsibility, etc.\n\nCandidate A: quick correct decisions (good decision quality), excellent attention (attention accuracy), puts concern for others (cooperation), but difficulty communicating ideas (communication issue), egocentric (cooperation/crew), not willing to further education (adaptability). So mixed.\n\nCandidate B: very conscientious (reliability), handles stress well (stress resilience), good at assessing weather (technical competence), excellent computer skills (technical), but pretentious and wrong tone (communication, crew cooperation). So strong reliability and stress, but communication concerns.\n\nCandidate C: anticipates dangerous situations (stress resilience, decision), sees complex connections (technical), excellent spatial vision (technical), very good leadership (crew cooperation), but unfriendly (crew), eats unhealthily (maybe health but not directly criteria). So strong technical and decision, but cooperation concerns.\n\nCandidate D: responds to unexpected events adequately (stress resilience), concentrates well (attention), solves problems extremely well (technical), takes responsibility seriously (responsibility), but moody and loner (crew cooperation). So strong responsibility, technical, but cooperation concerns.\n\nWe need to pick best overall fit, balancing strengths and concerns. All have some cooperation concerns. Which candidate has least concerning issues? B has pretentious and wrong tone, but is conscientious and handles stress. A has egocentric and communication difficulty, not willing to further education. C has unfriendly and unhealthy eating (maybe not relevant). D has moody and loner.\n\nWhich is most critical? Crew cooperation and communication are vital. B's communication issues may affect safety. A's egocentric may also be problematic. C's unfriendly may be problematic. D's moody/loner may affect teamwork.\n\nWe might consider B's strengths in reliability and stress handling outweigh communication concerns? Or D's responsibility and problem solving outweigh moody? Hard.\n\nWe need to start discussion, give a recommendation. Perhaps recommend Candidate B as leading due to high reliability, stress handling, technical competence, despite communication concerns that could be mitigated.\n\nLet's propose that. Provide evidence: very conscientious, handles stress well, good at assessing weather, but note pretentious and tone issues.\n\nThus vote for Candidate B.\n\nWe need to output PUBLIC_MESSAGE and METADATA_JSON.\n\nPublic message: brief argument, referencing facts, stating recommendation.\n\nProceed."}
